## S5 read-only slash commands in print mode (0 tokens)
$ -p /hooks   (temp home, no hooks) -> exit 0, empty
$ -p /permissions -> exit 0, empty
$ -p /context -> exit 2: error: /context is not available in print mode (it opens the interactive
  context breakdown); pass --disable-slash-commands to send /context to the model as literal text
$ -p /config -> exit 0, one key per line (the keys --settings accepts):


## S6 bundled extensions in a fresh root
$ agy agents -> exit 0, empty
$ agy mcp list -> No MCP servers configured.
$ agy plugin list -> No plugins installed.   (but /skills lists `swarm` from builtin/plugins)
$ agy --include-default-customizations=false … -> exit 2: flags provided but not defined
  (the flag exists only on `agy acp`, with --disable-telemetry and --login)
